WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
Glad you're with us on First Principles Daily, Episode 20.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.640
Today we reasoned from raw materials, not analogy.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.340
In 1941, the world's penicillin could treat only a handful of patients.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:15.640
Three years later, it covered every allied casualty on D-Day

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.100
because the process was rebuilt around oxygen transfer and reactor volume

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.180
instead of flask surface area.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.620
In the spring of 1941, a single patient in Oxford

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.480
received the entire British stock of penicillin.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.060
When the drug appeared in his urine, it was collected, purified again,

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:36.760
and given back to him because there was nothing else.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.900
Three years later, on the beaches of Normandy,

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:44.680
medical units carried enough penicillin to treat every wounded soldier who needed it.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.100
The molecule itself had not changed.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.920
What changed was the engineering that turned a few micrograms

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:55.360
per square centimeter of mold surface into kilograms per cubic meter

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.840
of tank volume every day.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:01.760
The shift required recognizing that the binding constraint was never the chemistry

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:06.160
of the beta-lactam ring, but the rate at which oxygen could be delivered

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:11.020
to the growing organism and the sheer volume that could be held sterile at one time.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.780
The original production method grew penicillium notatum on the surface

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:20.440
of a shallow liquid medium inside hundreds of individual flasks or bottles.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:25.240
Each vessel offered only a thin layer of air liquid interface.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.980
Oxygen reached the mold slowly and yield stayed low,

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.980
often measured in a few milligrams per liter.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:36.680
The approach copied standard microbiological laboratory practice.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:40.940
The goal had always been to obtain enough material for identification

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:45.240
and small animal tests rather than for thousands of human doses.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:49.640
Because every additional flask required more incubator space,

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:53.000
more manual handling, and more risk of contamination,

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:56.880
scaling simply meant building more of the same small units.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:01.040
The finished material therefore carried the full cost of that repetitive,

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.000
labor-intensive surface culture,

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.420
plus repeated extraction steps performed on tiny volumes.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.980
Early published accounts describe the drug as so scarce

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:13.140
that one course of treatment could cost the equivalent of several months

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.480
of a skilled worker's wages.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:19.340
No one inside the small research group questioned the flask geometry itself.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:22.540
It was the inherited tool for growing molds.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.900
The assumption was that any increase in supply would come from finding

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:30.280
a slightly better mold strain or a slightly richer broth,

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:33.300
while keeping the same surface culture format.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:37.740
That assumption fixed both the physical limit and the cost structure

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:41.180
until the problem was handed to groups whose daily work involved

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:44.300
large volume fluid handling rather than petri dishes.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:48.500
The surface method also locked in downstream bottlenecks.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:52.200
Each small batch had to be filtered, extracted with solvent,

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.020
and concentrated separately.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:59.260
This multiplied the number of transfer steps and the opportunities for loss or contamination.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:03.800
Because the flask could not be pressurized or vigorously agitated

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:08.440
without breaking the surface film, the organism never reached high cell densities.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:14.640
The same sugar and nitrogen inputs therefore produced far less product per kilogram consumed.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.840
The convention persisted because microbiologists had spent decades

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:22.240
perfecting exactly this format for studying metabolism.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:27.240
The idea that the same organism might behave differently once oxygen supply

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:31.380
was decoupled from surface area was outside the frame of reference.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:35.500
The decisive shift began when the question was restated as

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:39.980
how much penicillin can we produce per unit volume of reactor per day

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:43.800
if oxygen transfer, not surface area, sets the rate.

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:49.040
Deep tanks submerged fermentation replaced the flasks with sealed, stirred,

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.700
aerated vessels of thousands of liters.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:55.700
In these tanks, air was forced through spargers at the bottom

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:58.820
while mechanical agitators kept the broth mixed.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:04.600
Oxygen therefore dissolved throughout the liquid rather than only at the top surface.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:08.320
A rough magic wand estimate starts with the major inputs.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:14.420
Corn steep liquor, a cheap byproduct of wet milling, supplied nitrogen and growth factors

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:18.120
at commodity prices on the order of a few cents per kilogram.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:23.780
Lactose or glucose provided carbon at similarly low agricultural prices.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.780
Mineral salts added negligible cost.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:33.680
The penicillin molecule itself contains only carbon, hydrogen, nitrogen, oxygen, and sulfur.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:37.400
All drawn from those inexpensive feedstocks.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:42.260
Adding the energy for aeration, agitation, and downstream solvent extraction

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:47.700
still leaves a raw material floor that is a small fraction of even the later bulk drug price.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:53.140
Under the old surface culture regime, the finished costs at many times higher than that floor.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:58.240
This produced an idiot index that reflected the multiplication of small vessels,

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:02.660
repeated manual transfers, and low volumetric productivity

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:04.760
rather than any scarcity of atoms.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:10.480
To see the index clearly, consider that the raw atoms might cost a few cents per dose,

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:16.120
while the finished material required the labor of hundreds of flasks, each handled separately.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:20.880
The ratio of finished price to raw material costs therefore grew large

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:26.540
because every added flask multiplied the handling steps without increasing the volume per step.

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:33.260
Switching to deep tanks immediately raised the volume that could be processed in one vessel by orders of magnitude,

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.380
and eliminated most of the flask handling labor.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:43.640
The second move replaced the original low yielding strain with isolates from a moldy cantaloupe collected in peoria.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:52.040
Those strains produced several times more penicillin per gram of sugar consumed once they were grown under submerged conditions.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:59.080
The third move introduced deliberate mutation and selection programs that further increased the biosynthetic rate

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.500
without changing the medium chemistry.

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:05.040
Each of these steps attacked a different term in the same equation.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:10.240
Oxygen transfer rate, biomass density, and specific productivity.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:16.240
The engineering trade-off that had to be solved was maintaining sterility at large scale

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:20.240
while delivering sufficient power to the agitators and compressors.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:27.060
Once that mechanical problem was controlled, the biology scaled with the hardware instead of against it.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:32.740
One obvious objection is that larger vessels simply multiply contamination risk.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:39.180
Yet the teams addressed this by adopting the same clean-and-place and steam sterilization practices

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:42.220
already routine in brewing and dairy processing.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:49.440
Another objection is that the new strains might lose productivity under the higher shear of mechanical stirring.

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:58.300
In practice, the selected mutants proved more robust precisely because the selection pressure included the submerged environment itself.

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:05.840
The arithmetic of the idiot index therefore moved because the dominant cost term changed from number of flasks

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:11.140
times labor per flask to capital cost of tank plus energy per cubic meter.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:14.560
That quantity falls as volume increases.

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:25.740
By the middle of 1944, submerged fermentation plants were producing penicillin at a rate that made the drug available for every allied casualty who reached a clearing station.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:33.900
Published wartime production figures show output rising from kilograms per month to tons per month within roughly two years.

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:43.680
The idiot index of the process fell sharply because the dominant costs shifted from repetitive small scale handling to the capital cost of tanks and compressors.

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:48.020
Those costs could then be amortized over far larger volumes.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:08:02.540
The remaining gap to the absolute raw material floor is still set by the energy required for aeration and the losses in extraction and purification, both of which are governed by physical chemistry rather than by the number of flasks.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:09.780
Trade-offs accepted along the way included the need for highly trained operators to keep large sterile systems running

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:14.000
and the capital intensity of building the first deep tank facilities.

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:20.380
Those constraints were real, yet they proved far less limiting than the original surface culture ceiling.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:29.200
Even after the wartime effort, downstream solvent extraction and crystallization still accounted for a sizable fraction of the remaining cost.

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:36.200
The molecule had to be separated from a complex broth without degrading the sensitive beta-lactam ring.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:48.880
The new limit was therefore no longer how many flasks could be tended by hand, but how efficiently the dissolved oxygen could be converted into product and how completely the product could be recovered.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:09:01.600
When the limiting step is oxygen delivery into liquid rather than the number of glass surfaces, the entire cost structure moves with the reactor design instead of with laboratory tradition.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:15.420
When a growth medium is treated as an engineered fluid whose composition can be taken from an adjacent industry, the atom stop being the scarce resource and the mixing equipment becomes the variable that can still be improved.

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:29.160
The same reframing that turned penicillin from a urine recycling rarity into a standard issue medicine now sits in front of any process whose daily output is still measured in the same small vessels that first revealed the molecule.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:39.480
Which current high-value fermentation or cell culture product still carries an idiot index set by surface area instead of by the physics of gas transfer.

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:41.900
That's first principles daily for today.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:48.540
If this changed how you see what things cost, share it with someone who'd appreciate it and subscribe wherever you listen.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:54.560
I'm Patrick and Vancouver, one example or one opportunity every day. See you tomorrow.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:10:03.020
And if you'd rather watch then listen, find us on YouTube at NEH-RA network, links in the show notes.

